IV. Conclusions
In this study, a detailed mathematical model and systematic algorithm have been developed to obtain the trim conditions of a helicopter under any general maneuvering flight condition. Using this model, the trim conditions of a helicopter under a steady turn maneuver were analyzed. It was shown that the trim states could be evaluated by imposing any one of the three mathematical conditions, namely, zero sideslip, zero flight track angle, and zero lateral load factor. 1) The trim results corresponding to zero sideslip and zero track angle cases are almost same. But, the zero lateral load factor case is completely different from the other two cases. 2) It is shown that, under a few specific flight conditions, any two among the three mathematical conditions can be satisfied simultaneously. By imposing simultaneously the conditions of a 90 deg sideslip angle and a zero lateral load factor, a pirouettelike flight condition can be achieved. For the first time in the open literature, a mathematical condition for the pirouette maneuver of a helicopter has been identified. 3) The zero lateral load factor condition cannot be satisfied at all the advance ratios.
